From 7f95eb07d3774b3ccd1ce8b2336179071a802a52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xenos <xenos@localhost>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:17:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 04/22] freedreno/a2xx: Xbox 360 Xenos variant (gpu_id 290)

New device entry (chip 0x02090000, 10MB GMEM = EDRAM, bins aligned to 160x16 so the
EDRAM pitch is an even number of 80x16 tiles) and a drm-shim entry. On Xenos:
- render-target registers use the Xenos layout: EDRAM bases in tiles, no a2xx
  format/swap fields (fd2_xenos.h); RB_SURFACE_INFO pitch only
- resolve: Xenos RB_COPY_CONTROL (convert), RB_COPY_DEST_PITCH (pitch|height<<16),
  RB_COPY_DEST_INFO (format, endian and R/B swap per pipe format, measured on hw)
- single bin (EDRAM holds 720p color+depth), no RB_COPY_DEST_OFFSET
- no a2xx perfmon/PM_OVERRIDE/TP0_CHICKEN/TC_CNTL_STATUS writes; cache invalidate via
  the COHER_*_HOST sequence libxenon uses; no SET_DRAW_INIT_FLAGS / WAIT_REG_EQ
- MEM_WRITE split to one dword per packet (Xenos stores only the first)
- always render through EDRAM (no sysmem path for batches that draw)
- render formats limited to 8888 (incl. big-endian ARGB/ABGR variants), depth D24S8
The resulting command streams pass xegpu's kernel command checker under drm-shim.

